WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
A value can have the correct data type and still be wrong.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:08.952
For example, negative twenty is a valid number in Python.

00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:15.707
But if the variable represents a purchase amount, a negative value may violate a business rule.

00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:23.822
A satisfaction score of nine is also numeric, but it is invalid if the allowed scale is one through five.

00:00:24.604 --> 00:00:27.061
This is why domain knowledge matters.

00:00:27.061 --> 00:00:35.216
Run the code and notice that we create Boolean conditions to flag invalid values rather than deleting them

00:00:35.216 --> 00:00:37.711
automatically. That is an important workflow.

00:00:37.711 --> 00:00:45.436
First detect the problem, then inspect the affected rows, and only then decide what action is appropriate.

00:00:45.436 --> 00:00:53.546
Business rules are often more useful than generic statistical rules because they reflect what the data is supposed to

00:00:53.546 --> 00:00:58.893
mean. Always ask whether a value is possible in the real process that generated the data.
